  "summary": "The study fabricated five electrochemically compared Ti3C2Tx film electrodes: pristine p-MF, annealed a-MF, and three gelatin-derived carbon-dot intercalated films (CDs-MF-1/-2/-3) made using 3%, 5%, and 10 wt.% gelatin, respectively. MXene was synthesized by LiF/HCl etching and the CD-containing films were carbonized at 400 \u00b0C under Ar. CDs-MF-2 was the headline and best gravimetric performer, reaching 396.4 F g-1 at 1 A g-1 and 1,153.2 F cm-3 at 1 A cm-3 in 3 M H2SO4. CDs-MF-1 delivered the highest explicitly stated volumetric capacitance, 1,347.0 F cm-3 at 1 A cm-3. Mass loading, BET surface area, pore-size distribution, porosity percentage, and tortuosity were not reported; the conclusion's assignment of volumetric values to CDs-MF-2/-3 conflicts with the detailed Results text, which assigns 1,347.0 F cm-3 to CDs-MF-1."
}